Is this subject really a dental/oral responsibility? In recent years, snoring and sleep apnea have become associated with dentists, and many dentists are finding that some aspects of this topic will be useful in general practice. It is estimated that at least 30 to 50 percent of the U.S. population snores. You may already know of potentially interested patients in your own practice. Dr. DiTolla has personally seen a few very difficult responses to patients who asked the simple question, “Would you like to hear how your spouse’s snoring may be treated without surgery?” However, more serious than snoring is the potentially life-threatening condition named Obstructive Sleep Apnea, estimated to be present in 1 to 4 percent of severity in one in 15 adults. This DVD emphasizes the methods to reduce or eliminate snoring and how to implement the techniques into typical dental practice. Advice is also provided on diagnosis of sleep apnea and potential treatments for this potentially dangerous condition.

